{
  "item": "GiantOgre01",
  "mu_name": "Giant Ogre",
  "mu_name_from": "MuMain _enum.h MONSTER_GIANT_OGRE_1 (87), drawn as MODEL_GIANT_OGRE = MODEL_MONSTER01 + 58, so OpenMonsterModel loads Monster59.bmd; the client's name is 자이언트오우거, 'giant ogre' (ZzzCharacter.cpp:13495). WebZen's Monster.txt:115 calls breed 87 'Spirit Beast'; MuMain's English client and OpenMU S6 BloodCastle1.cs call it Giant Ogre. docs/blood-castle-port.md Part B 3.",
  "world": "bloodcastle",
  "object_type": 87,
  "monster": {
    "model_index": 58,
    "scale": 0.8
  },
  "monster_from": "ZzzCharacter.cpp:13485-13496, CreateMonster, case MONSTER_GIANT_OGRE_1..8: OpenMonsterModel(MONSTER_MODEL_GIANT_OGRE); CreateCharacter(Key, MODEL_GIANT_OGRE, ...); Scale = 0.8f. No weapon, no BlendMesh. Its ranged attack: WebZen's attack type is 17 (Monster.txt:115), but what MuMain draws (MoveCharacterVisual's attack switch, ZzzCharacter.cpp:2090-2105) is MODEL_FIRE subtype 5 from bone 6, a ball of fire flying straight out at 30 units a frame for 40 frames (ZzzEffect.cpp:2580-2584) -- so its attack_skill here is Fire Ball (4), not Energy Ball's orb.",
  "profile": "monster",
  "rig_from": "Eight actions, exported with --actions=all. 70 bones, 1,934 triangles -- the heaviest body in the castle.",
  "sheets": {
    "st091": "giantogre_st091.png"
  },
  "sheet_from": "One sheet, Data/Monster/st091.OZJ, 256x256, no alpha, on all 1,934 triangles. Decoded under a giantogre_ prefix.",
  "sheet_materials": {
    "st091": "skin"
  },
  "sheet_materials_from": "Read off the sheet at 2x: a black, glistening hide over a lizard's body, spined and studded, red-eyed; at the top left a strip of flame-orange teeth or claws, painted, which MU does not make glow. All skin, the monster profile's own.",
  "islands_from": "All skin, as they arrive: the sheet is hide throughout.",
  "sounds_from": "ZzzOpenData.cpp:3809-3813: mHunter2 and mGhaintOrgerDie, SetMonsterSound(..., 188, -1, 190, -1, 191) -- offsets from SOUND_MONSTER_BULL1 = 210: 398 HUNTER2_ to walk, 401 GHAINTORGERDIE to die (DSPlaySound.h:338-342). Its attack slot 400 is BLACKSKULLATTACK, which this model does not load: it sounds in MU because the Dark Skull Soldier, in the same castle, loads it -- so the Dark Skull's attack here too. Wired as giantogre_* in sounds.json.",
